{%- comment -%}
  The sale badge for one price: its text, or nothing. The theme's one rule for
  showing a sale, and it is Shopify's: a product is on sale when its compare-at
  price is above its price. Put products on sale (or take them off) in Shopify,
  one by one, by collection, or all at once; the site follows.

  The wording is content: global.json "sale_badge" "text" ("Sale"), which a
  look can change, e.g. to "[percent]% OFF" — [percent] is that product's
  saving from its Shopify prices ("50% OFF").

  The same rule runs in the browser as window.ScentspiredSale (layout/theme.liquid).

  Usage:
    {%- capture badge -%}{% render 'sale--badge', price: variant.price, compare_at_price: variant.compare_at_price %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if compare_at_price > price
    capture badge_text
      render 'region--content', key: 'global.sale_badge.text'
    endcapture
    assign saving_percent = compare_at_price | minus: price | times: 100 | divided_by: compare_at_price
    echo badge_text | strip | replace: '[percent]', saving_percent
  endif
-%}
